# Maintainer: Yūrei Linux project
# Yūrei's own recipe (stage 3, the desktop; docs/INDEPENDENT.md). The source
# address and sum are the ones in independent/bootstrap/sources.lock;
# check-recipes.py keeps them the same.
pkgname=libdisplay-info
pkgver=0.2.0
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc="Reads what a monitor says about itself (EDID)"
arch=(x86_64)
url="https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/emersion/libdisplay-info"
license=(MIT)
depends=(glibc)
source=("https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/emersion/libdisplay-info/-/releases/$pkgver/downloads/libdisplay-info-$pkgver.tar.xz")
sha256sums=('5a2f002a16f42dd3540c8846f80a90b8f4bdcd067a94b9d2087bc2feae974176')

build() {
    meson setup libdisplay-info-$pkgver build --prefix=/usr --buildtype=release
    ninja -C build
}

package() {
    DESTDIR="$pkgdir" ninja -C build install
}
